ay if I don't do this now  you might not ever do it or you might a  couple years down the road regret having  not tried or not gone for that or taking  a risk essentially so I took the risk  and drop that a high score call it and  enlisted on a few months later we  and my parents were really proud of me  at that point in the beginning they  weren't and then as I left and went  through the process and and I made it  through the training the training is six  months long and often times going  through it people get hurt or rolled  back for performance so you stay there  for a really long time but I was able to  make it through in one in one iteration  which was I was very fortunate and then  so my 20s that entire time I was  stationed mostly in Virginia that's the  phase of my life I don't talk much about  but it's really formative of Who I am  now and what I do now the the decade  twelve years that I was in the Navy and  I don't talk a lot about it because you  know we were the silent professional  that's how we were brought up we were  not supposed to talk about what we did  and I really took that to heart and I I  was raised in that community by guys who  were that I really respected that kind  of beat that mentality into you that hey  you're a Navy SEAL you're not supposed  to talk about what you do  [Music]  you
 

